721:Normative modelling has some key advantages over alternative approaches  to  quantifying  atrophy  relative  to  a  reference  group,  for example using W-score metrics, which have been previously applied to PD and DLB (Tremblay et al., 2021; Spotorno et al., 2020). The reference dataset of 58,836 used in normative modelling is around a thousand-fold larger  than  most W-score reference datasets, capturing much greater population variability and providing more robust estimates of deviation from control data. Further, the neuroanatomical normative modelling pipeline enables inter-individual heterogeneity to be quantified, which is not usually examined using W-score approaches.
